  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 1, 2, 6, 7, 9, 10, 14, 15, 16, 20, 22 (one guarded start with its bounded wait; SSH preparation only when converging; one end check, no digest re-check or result print).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · a workspace operation wakes the VM
  %% kind: task_vm.resume
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane VM icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant H as Task VM host<br/>Node 13 over ssh
  participant VM as Task VM<br/>tvm-333 over ssh
  Note over GW: Validate, record the task<br/>task VM 333 · task #5181 · Node 13
  %%> Started by:
  %%> - `WakeTaskVmAction`, when a workspace operation needs parked VM 333 or finds a `ready` VM stopped
  %%> - the operator command `task-vms:resume 333` on the Gateway; there is no orbit CLI command
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - task VM 333 is `parked`, or `ready` for a convergence
  %%> - no other task holds `task_vm:333`; a repeated admission returns the same open task
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5181 records the host, the VM, guest Node 340, its recorded host key pin and mode `resume` or `converge`
  %%> - clears the stop proof; for UpCloud, a vault copy of the API token
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-vm-resume
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the intent and `execution_secrets` as vault key names
  %%> - the input schema validates the intent; no `eligible` assert re-checks it (rule 15)
  SW->>H: Start the VM<br/>provider · incus start · wait
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one argv on Node 13: `incus start tvm-333`, then `incus wait tvm-333 agent --timeout 120`
  %%> - a `guard` skips the start when the VM already runs (rule 20)
  %%> Per provider:
  %%> - UpCloud overflow: the API start from 209, with the token from the vault, then one bounded observation
  %%> Replaces:
  %%> - `input`, `incus-before`, `before`, `incus-action`, `incus-after` and `result` of `task-vm-provider-power`
  opt VM was ready (converge)
    SW->>VM: Converge 209 SSH access<br/>ssh · authorized key · TCP 22
    %%> When:
    %%> - mode `converge`; a parked VM kept its SSH access on its disk, so a resume skips this (rule 1)
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - one pinned exec each for 209's authorized key, the TCP 22 rule for 209 and `sshd`
    %%> Replaces:
    %%> - the `task-vm-ssh-prepare` child; `package` and `host-keys` belong to provision (rule 2)
    Note over SW: open: Nick decides<br/>converge as its own kind?
    %%> Why:
    %%> - convergence of a running VM shares this kind today; it is not a resume
  end
  SW->>VM: Check the guest is ready<br/>check · agent, Pi capabilities
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one pinned exec over WireGuard reads `orbit-agent` status and the Pi capabilities with the Pi token file; Swamp's `assert` checks them
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - the Pi build digest check: the parked disk holds the build that provision proved (rule 1)
  %%> Replaces:
  %%> - `artifact`, `pi`, `runtime-confirmed` and the `result` print (rules 9, 14)
  alt every step passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>tvm-333 ready
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its run reader sees the terminal event and reads the `check` step's outputs
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task VM 333 is `ready`; the waiting workspace operation goes on
    %%> - task #5181 succeeds
  else a step fails
    VM--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or timeout
    %%> When:
    %%> - the VM does not start within 120 seconds, or the agent or Pi does not answer
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task #5181 fails; a parked VM 333 becomes `failed` with the error
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - the VM may stay running; there is no rollback
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - a failed VM stays final; the group asks for assistance, and `tasks:cancel` destroys the VM
  end
